.Dd November 7, 2026
.Dt TASKPOLICY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm taskpolicy
.Nd run a program with a scheduling and I/O policy
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl x | Fl X
.Op Fl d Ar policy
.Op Fl g Ar policy
.Op Fl c Ar clamp
.Op Fl b
.Op Fl t Ar tier
.Op Fl l Ar tier
.Op Fl a
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl S Ar shims
.Op Fl P Ar control
.Op Fl m Ar limit
.Op Fl j Ar priority
.Ar program Op Ar argument ...
.Nm
.Op Fl b | Fl B
.Op Fl t Ar tier
.Op Fl l Ar tier
.Fl p Ar pid
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
applies a policy, then runs
.Ar program
in its place.
With
.Fl p ,
it changes a running process instead.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl x
Force case-sensitive HFS lookups.
.It Fl X
Use the default case sensitivity for HFS lookups.
.It Fl d Ar policy
Set the disk I/O policy of the process.
.It Fl g Ar policy
Set the disk I/O policy used in the background state.
.It Fl c Ar clamp
Limit the quality of service to
.Cm utility ,
.Cm background
or
.Cm maintenance .
.It Fl b
Put the process in the background state.
.It Fl B
Take the process out of the background state.
.It Fl t Ar tier
Set the throughput tier.
.It Fl l Ar tier
Set the latency tier.
.It Fl a
Mark the program as an application.
.It Fl s
Start the program suspended.
.It Fl S Ar shims
Set the security transition shims.
.It Fl P Ar control
Set what happens under resource pressure:
.Cm throttle ,
.Cm kill
or
.Cm suspend .
.It Fl m Ar limit
Set a fatal memory limit, in MiB.
.It Fl j Ar priority
Set the memory pressure priority.
.It Fl p Ar pid
Change this process.
.El
.Pp
A disk I/O
.Ar policy
is a number, or one of
.Cm default ,
.Cm important ,
.Cm passive ,
.Cm throttle ,
.Cm utility
or
.Cm standard .
